  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1239 PM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nThe forecast is staying on track from the last few issuances. \nMid-level high pressure will continue to build over the next \ncouple of days from the east and is still expected to take over \nby midweek. Expect this to promote warm and mostly rain free \nconditions outside of seabreeze convection. Will need to monitor \nthe possibility for some short-fused heat related products. We \ncould see heat indices up to 115 as early as tomorrow with dew \npoints around the mid to upper 70s present through the next week. \nThis translates to Moderate to Major heat stress conditions though\nwe could see some areas reach Extreme conditions by Thursday. We \nstrongly encourage the practice of heat safety in these \nconditions. Take frequent breaks and remember to stay hydrated, \ncheck those backseats, and avoid long exposure in these \ntemperatures. For more information be sure to check out \nweather.gov/heatsafety.",
